+
+// The write-surface gate for the repo-side growth runs (extract, dedup): the
+// extract PR auto-merges with no human review, so the boundary needs a machine
+// guarantee, not a prose request. A growth run announces itself with a commit
+// subject starting "Claudinite growth:" (its skill pins the title); when a
+// branch carries such a commit, the change must fit the surface:
+//
+//   - under .claudinite/local/packs/ (legacy .claudinite/local_packs/ accepted
+//     during the rename window): anything — the local packs are the capture
+//     surface, add/modify/delete freely;
+//   - everywhere else: ONLY whole comment lines inserted into existing files —
+//     the usage-site gotcha extract's method mandates ("a comment right at the
+//     call site"). No rewritten or removed lines, no new files, no deletions:
+//     an insertion-only comment diff cannot change behavior, which is what
+//     makes it safe to land unreviewed.
+//
+// Sibling of canon-curation's promote-scope gate (the canon-side write
+// surface). Promote can't self-gate — nothing in a diff marks it as a promote
+// run, so CI keys on its branch prefix — but a growth run marks ITSELF via the
+// pinned commit subject, so this rule self-gates and runs everywhere the pack
+// is active: at the session Stop hook (work scope), and as a CLI on every PR
+// in the canon repo's CI (via canon-curation's growth-scope-gate.mjs there).
+//
+// Local packs live under either root during the rename transition; git emits
+// '/'-separated paths, so the platform-joined constants are normalized.
+const LOCAL_ROOTS = [LOCAL_PACKS_SUBDIR, LEGACY_LOCAL_PACKS_SUBDIR]
+  .map((s) => `${s.split(sep).join('/')}/`);
+
+const GROWTH_RUN = /^Claudinite growth:/;
