19://   a MIGRATION RECORD  — migrations/active_migrations/<date>-<name>.mjs, the
20-//                         mechanism that rewrites a member on its next converge
21://   a REHEARSAL FIXTURE — packs-tests/rehearsal/fixtures.mjs, which proves a
22-//                         consumer in that shape still converges green
23-//
24-// Either satisfies it. They answer different questions — "members are moved
25-// across" versus "members are unharmed" — and both are legitimate; a change that
26-// is genuinely additive needs only the second.
27-//
28-// DELIBERATELY NARROW. It triggers on three surfaces, each chosen because a
29-// consumer holds a copy of it and cannot be asked to change in the same commit:
30-//
31-//   pack-schema.mjs        the manifest vocabulary — #555's exact surface
32-//   a rule's `severity`    advisory -> blocking turns a member red overnight
33-//   the scheduler stub     every member vendors it verbatim
34-//
35-// It does NOT fire on ordinary pack or engine edits. A rule that cried wolf on
36-// every canon commit would be turned off within a week, and then it would be
37-// worth nothing on the day it mattered.
38-const SCHEMA = 'engine/pack_loader/pack-schema.mjs';
39-const STUB = 'engine/scheduler/stubs/claudinite-scheduler.yml';
40:const MIGRATIONS = 'migrations/active_migrations/';
41:const FIXTURES = 'packs-tests/rehearsal/fixtures.mjs';
